  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 134 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nToday through Wed night...The bulk of precipitation ends prior \nto forecast start at 0500 MST this morning. Some lingering \nshowers over the highlands bordering WY should end during the \nafternoon. Clouds will clear for tonight and the main risk \ntonight will be BR/FG and stratus clouds. \n\nTemperatures today will struggle into the upper 40s at lower\nelevations. The cool end to the afternoon means chilly\ntemperatures under nearly clear skies: Teens in the alpine\nbasins, mid-20s to low 30s for the Snake River plain/eastern\nMagic Valley, 20s for the highlands. The abundant sunshine will\nput both highs and lows on a warming trend for Tue. Cloud cover\non Wed/Wed night will cool highs and level off overnight lows.\nThe cloud cover comes from a low moving through UT.\n\n\nWindy conditions this morning in the post-frontal zone will\nsubside during the afternoon as the upper level support for\nstrong wind diminishes. \n\nThu through Sun...Building upper level high pushes storm track\nfarther north and away from southern ID. The ridge axis staying\nto the west will mean northwest air flow and a re-supply of cold\nair that will keep temperatures from warming too strongly, or\neven leveling off until Sun. On Sun, a low off the west coast\nshifts wind to more southerly and temperatures will warm more\nstrongly.",
